# D158 (2): the submission race is fixed. This file IS the evidence, not a flag.
#
# Fix: sent_bytes_for was doing two jobs and the set is split. sent_bytes_for still advances at
# SUBMISSION and still drives BUILD PROGRESS, so no decision moves. New confirmed_bytes_for
# advances only on HTTP 200 and drives REFERENCE ELIGIBILITY. The dashcam side is split the same
# way (_mon_sent / _mon_confirmed), which the brief did not name but the data demanded: the
# saturated cell was 1,113 dashcam 400s against 397 robot. Pieces are NOT serialised.
#
# THE THREE PROOFS D158 (2) REQUIRED, all passing:
#   1.  50-arm prescreen before/after at the same commit: 50 of 50 byte-identical, 0 errors
#   1b. the same claim on a cell with a REAL frame store: digests identical both arms, both
#       regimes, frames_sent identical at 2,205 and 1,922
#   2.  body-level diff: 439 of 7,060 bodies change, 0 for any other reason, 0 with no bare
#       reference
#   3.  CAL1F replay: 226 of 226 failures carried a reference to unacknowledged bytes under the
#       old rule, 0 under the new
#   tests: 152 of 152, identical to baseline, including D153's epg_bodies_proof
#
# PROOF 1 AS ORIGINALLY SPECIFIED WAS VACUOUS, which is why 1b exists. baseline_prescreen passes
# no frames_root, so _path returns None for every frame, sent_bytes_for never grows, and the
# quantity the fix branches on is EMPTY. Proof 1 alone proves decision-identity in a regime where
# no frame carries bytes. That is the same false-proof shape already recorded for EP-G's proof (a),
# and it was caught at Step 0 rather than after the sweep.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TREATING THE RACE AS CLOSED. A dangerous reference is NECESSARY for the 400 but
# NOT SUFFICIENT: 226 of 226 failures carried one, and so did 517 of 957 SUCCESSES. So the engine
# registers some images before the carrying request returns, and the 200 is a later moment than the
# one that actually matters. Proof 3 therefore bounds the fix FROM ONE SIDE ONLY: it removes the
# condition present in 100 percent of failures. It does NOT establish that those 226 would now
# return 200. Only D158 (3)'s re-run settles that, and the _rf cells are what decide it.
#
# COST, which is larger than "uplink rises" suggests, because an unconfirmed frame is re-sent:
#   warm-all-lru declared cell   737.4 MB to 1,147.6 MB   x1.556
#   CAL1F sequence               4,323 to 34,535 image parts carrying bytes   x7.99
#   edf                          no change   x1.000, because it has no in-flight overlap and so
#                                never had the race
# Prompt tokens are NOT claimed to rise: a re-sent frame keeps its mm_uuid, so the engine's
# multimodal cache key is unchanged and est_tokens does not move. Whether the engine re-prefills a
# re-sent image or serves it from its mm cache needs a live cell, and that is the one open cost.
#
# Any EP-G cell quoting epg_frames_sent_as_reference or _as_bytes must say which side of this fix
# it is on: those counters count the WIRE, which is what their names claim, so their values move.
